{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1123637-werewolves-in-woods","id":1123637,"title":"Werewolves in woods","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-01T14:34:30-07:00","id":1123637,"title":"Werewolves in woods","content":"<b>So this may seems strange question, but what Forsaken Tribes could live in woods?</b> Of course first answer could be Hunters in Darkness \u2013 as most Nature related Tribe \u2013 but this time it does not work with storyline in my mind. Countered they are probably by Predator Kings, those Uratha most devoted to eschewing civilisation \u2013 but those are Pure.<br /> <br /> I have Viking Era plotline around year 800 A.D. about massacred Forsaken pack ( Bale Hounds, in reality ) that live \u2018as wolves\u2019 in forest near Iona monastery. Most logical would be to use Hunters in Darkness \u2013 BUT I need this rest of pack to join my Forsaken Viking PCs.<br /> <br /> <i>Meninna</i> are rather obsessive on guarding one place \u2013 <i>&quot;Let No Sacred Place in Your Territory Be Violated&quot;</i> \u2013 and I cannot see them just leaving their original Territory when PCs come. So I look for other Tribe of Moon that could like living in woods.<br /> <br /> Even if I love Iron Masters myself, I would try to miss them on this subject \u2013 Masters are \u2018civilization werewolves\u2019 in my games, and I try to stick to it. They also hunts humans, so in woods they would not have many Sacred Preys.<br /> <br /> Storm Lords are all about showing and expressing inner strength \u2013 and living in forest is much more harder than in villages. Also, Spirit-Urged or Claimed can easily be humans OR animals. I think that <i>Iminir </i>hunting \u2018monstrous spiders\u2019 ( not Azlu ) or \u2018royal animals\u2019 ( semi-Pangeans made from superClaimed ) is more than viable in woods setting. They are loners \u2013 on \u2018not showing weakness\u2019 side \u2013 but they also want to lead and going to foreign land, when you lose your own battles, maybe answer here? There is also thread of that his massacre was made by vampires using humans in battle with local pack \u2013 and Storm Lords are known to \u2018mistaken\u2019 other monsters for next Claimed they need to hunt \u2013 so it\u2019s next plotline reason to use them.<br /> <br /> Blood Talons are everywhere where other werewolves are. I could use them in woods setting, but they do not seems are any more appropriate as other Tribes. On the other hand, <i>Suthar Anzuth</i> are more about proper WAR than simple hunting \u2013 and this is somehow more human thing, easier to be done in civilized lands. They can be backup plan.<br /> <br /> Bone Shadows are everywhere where are dead or secrets \u2013 early Middle Ages woods have plenty of both, so <i>Hirfathra Hissu </i>could be my answer. They also are most curious of they kind, so easily would hop on boats with PCs. And worshiping dark powers is really only question of point of view. It\u2019s so good pick, I\u2019m worried it\u2019s <i>too easy</i> choice.<br /> <br /> <b>So I want to hear your thoughts on those \u2013 I now wonder mostly on using Storm Lords or Bone Shadows.</b> Lords seems to make good opportunity to show Tribe in it\u2019s strong and weak side \u2013 but I\u2019m still consider they eagerness to travel, even in eyes of obvious defeat. Bone Shadows are just ( maybe ) too easy pick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T14:41:26-07:00","id":1123642,"title":"","content":"Iron Masters might live in the woods and just watch over humanity from afar, only intervening when they really need to.<br /> <br /> If Predator Kings live in the woods there's no reason Blood Talons shouldn't.<br /> <br /> I mean, really, anyone could live in the woods. The only tribe that's hard to imagine living in the woods is the Ivory Claws, because they have a sort of 'above everyone else' type of thing going for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T14:57:30-07:00","id":1123646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1123637-werewolves-in-woods?p=1123642#post1123642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iron Masters might live in the woods and just watch over humanity from afar, only intervening when they really need to.<br /> <br /> If Predator Kings live in the woods there's no reason Blood Talons shouldn't.<br /> <br /> I mean, really, anyone could live in the woods. The only tribe that's hard to imagine living in the woods is the Ivory Claws, because they have a sort of 'above everyone else' type of thing going for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotta put your estates somewhere away from the unwashed masses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T15:29:29-07:00","id":1123660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1123637-werewolves-in-woods?p=1123646#post1123646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gotta put your estates somewhere away from the unwashed masses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. But even in just 'wilderness' you can still have a prime spot of some sort.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://1.bp.blogspot.com/-5Qme62pTReg/V0u8As5vr9I/AAAAAAAAhgY/KXSAof_41UIVE5SM67I9HL6byTcl1QKQwCLcB/s1600/%25E9%259B%25BB%25E5%25BD%25B1%25E8%25A7%2580%25E5%25BE%258C%25E5%2588%2586%25E4%25BA%25AB%25EF%25BC%259A%25E8%25BF%25AA%25E5%25A3%25AB%25E5%25B0%25BC%25E3%2580%258A%25E9%25AD%2594%25E5%25B9%25BB%25E6%25A3%25AE%25E6%259E%2597%25E3%2580%258B%2B%25283%2529.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-01-2017, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T17:14:46-07:00","id":1123710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1123637-werewolves-in-woods?p=1123642#post1123642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Predator Kings live in the woods there's no reason Blood Talons shouldn't..</div> </div> </div> </div>This exact thought occurred to me as well. That would mean penciling in a nearby Predator King or other Pure pack for the Blood Talons to be fighting, perhaps Ivory Claws have the local villages firmly in their control and the Blood Talons have to fight from the wilderness against the civilized Pure and their wolf blooded pack members. Clearing out the local Pure problem would be a great motivator to get Blood Talons to move to places with more of their sacred prey...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png",